rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&rft.genre=unknown&rft.jtitle=archive.adaic.com&rft.atitle=Ada+83+Reference+Manual+%28raise+statement%29&rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Farchive.adaic.com%2Fstandards%2F83lrm%2Fhtml%2Flrm-11-03.html%2311.3&rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3APython+%28programming+language%29\"\n              - listitem [ref=e2443]:\n                - generic [ref=e2444]:\n                  - text: ^\n                  - link \"Jump up to:\" [ref=e2445] [cursor=pointer]:\n                    - /url: \"#cite_ref-98-interview_22-0\"\n                  - link [ref=e2447] [cursor=pointer]:\n                    - /url: \"#cite_ref-98-interview_22-1\"\n                - generic [ref=e2448]:\n                  - generic [ref=e2449]:\n                    - text: Kuchling, Andrew M. (22 December 2006).\n                    - link \"\\\"Interview with Guido van Rossum (July 1998)\\\"\" [ref=e2450] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - /url: https://web.archive.org/web/20070501105422/http://www.amk.ca/python/writing/gvr-interview\n                    - text: . amk.ca. Archived from\n                    - link \"the original\" [ref=e2451] [cursor=pointer]:\n                      - /url: http://www.amk.ca/python/writing/gvr-interview\n                    - text: on 1 May 2007\n                    - generic [ref=e2452]: . Retrieved 12 March 2012\n                    - text: . I'd spent a summer at DEC's Systems Research Center, which introduced me to Modula-2+; the Modula-3 final report was being written there at about the same time. What I learned there later showed up in Python's exception handling, modules, and the fact that methods explicitly contain 'self' in their parameter list. String slicing came from Algol-68 and Icon.\n                  - generic \"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&rft.genre=unknown&rft.jtitle=amk.ca&rft.atitle=Interview+with+Guido+van+Rossum+%28July+1998%29&rft.date=2006-12-22&rft.aulas